# GitHub workflow

This repo lives on GitHub: `git@github.com:itsuppartem/artek-buddy.git`.

| Branch | Role |
| --- | --- |
| `develop` | Daily work. Default branch. |
| `main` | Released product only. |

## Never

- Do not `git push` to `main` or `master`. Not even a fast-forward.
- Do not commit on `main`. If you are on `main`, switch to `develop` or a feature branch first.
- Do not open a feature PR against `main`.

## Flow

1. Branch from current `develop` (`feature/…` or `fix/…`).
2. Commit there. Push that branch. Open a pull request **into `develop`**.
3. A release is a pull request **`develop` → `main`**. Merge on GitHub. Never push `main`.
   That merge starts `release.yml` when `VERSION` changed. Only the five newest GitHub Releases are kept.

Small owner work may commit on `develop` and push `origin develop`. That is the only branch that may be pushed without a PR.

## After a finished change

1. Bump the one product version when behavior ships (`VERSION`, `src/artek_buddy/__init__.py`, `client/VERSION`).
2. Update `README.md` in the same change: version, what a user can do, install example (`.deb` filename), compose/env if those changed.
3. Follow [precommit-hygiene.mdc](precommit-hygiene.mdc). Do not commit secrets.

## Do not commit

`.env`, tokens, `*.deb`, `data/`, `scripts/`, `docs/`, `docker-compose.local.yml`. Attribution of the adapted Rakazo contracts stays in `README.md` / `NOTICE` only. Do not present this repo as their TypeScript port.

## Language

Commit messages and repo docs stay English. Chat with the user may stay in their language.
